C.5 Query Templates

The following Cypher queries implement common analytical operations on the graph.

Q1. Claims with the longest persistence time.

```cypher
MATCH (c:Claim)-[:HAS_VERSION]->(v:ClaimVersion)-[:HAS_STATE]->(s:StatusState)
WITH c, v, s
ORDER BY s.timestamp
WITH c, collect(s)[0] AS first_state, collect(s)[-1] AS last_state
WHERE first_state.p_supported > 0.7 AND last_state.p_refuted + last_state.p_superseded > 0.7
RETURN c.id, c.canonical_title,
       duration.between(first_state.timestamp, last_state.timestamp).years AS years_persisted
ORDER BY years_persisted DESC;
```

Q2. Claims with the smallest auxiliary belt.

```cypher
MATCH (c:Claim)-[:HAS_VERSION]->(v:ClaimVersion)-[:DEPENDS_ON]->(h:AuxiliaryHypothesis)
WITH c, v, count(h) AS belt_size
WHERE belt_size <= 1
RETURN c.id, c.canonical_title, belt_size;
```

Q3. Anomalies refuting multiple claims.

```cypher
MATCH (an:Anomaly)-[:ANOMALOUS_FOR]->(v:ClaimVersion)<-[:HAS_VERSION]-(c:Claim)
WITH an, collect(DISTINCT c.id) AS affected_claims
WHERE size(affected_claims) > 1
RETURN an.id, an.title, affected_claims;
```

Q4. Claims whose rivals dominate.

```cypher
MATCH (c:Claim)-[r:RIVALS]->(c2:Claim)
WHERE r.rivalry_strength > 0.7
MATCH (c2)-[:HAS_VERSION]->(v2:ClaimVersion)-[:HAS_STATE]->(s2:StatusState)
WHERE s2.p_supported > 0.6
RETURN c.id AS losing_claim, c2.id AS winning_rival, r.rivalry_strength;
```

